    "id": "ctkg:v3e-object-f2043c62f7852b9f7e0bb3a8",
    "canonicalType": "KnowledgeStatement",
    "label": "高于 ω_s/2（称为奈奎斯特频率）的频率，由于包含在 z=e^{s T} 中的三角函数的周期性特征，会在 z 平面上叠加在对应的较低频率之上。这种重叠称为混叠或折叠。因此，为了用采样信号表示原信号，采样速率必须至少是信号最高频率分量的两倍。",
    "aliases": [],
    "description": "Frequencies greater than ω_s/2, called the Nyquist frequency, appear in the z-plane on the top of corresponding lower frequencies because of the circular character of the trigonometric functions imbedded in z=e^{s T}. This overlap is called aliasing or folding. As a result it is necessary to sample at least twice as fast as a signal's highest frequency component in order to represent that signal with the samples.",
